{"id": "EUVD-2026-25556", "enisaUuid": "fd51b761-50d4-30a0-bc4c-54dcd75127dc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: hold dev ref until after transport_finish NF_HOOK\n\nAfter async crypto completes, xfrm_input_resume() calls dev_put()\nimmediately on re-entry before the skb reaches transport_finish.\nThe skb->dev pointer is then used inside NF_HOOK and its okfn,\nwhich can race with device teardown.\n\nRemove the dev_put from the async resumption entry and instead\ndrop the reference after the NF_HOOK call in transport_finish,\nusing a saved device pointer since NF_HOOK may consume the skb.\nThis covers NF_DROP, NF_QUEUE and NF_STOLEN paths that skip\nthe okfn.\n\nFor non-transport exits (decaps, gro, drop) and secondary\nasync return points, release the reference inline when\nasync is set.", "datePublished": "2026-04-24T14:45:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:39", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94439cbe478b53f92223da9aae95fffb28623c3f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4236c30b437b80f673b9e08c8fae38b8d471ac9e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f451b43c88bf2b9c038b414be580efee42e031b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5002beda5cac69d522dc54da0d5d463ed9c963d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c428b03840094410c5fb6a5db30640486bbbfcb"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v4m9-vrgr-8xm2", "CVE-2026-31663"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0848efe6-c2c0-3ede-a314-56985e0d9b68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "3a011ca0-5263-3995-ad90-0b109a0af966", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3c93e8b2-b4b1-3001-8235-55a522cccd17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "acf568ee859f098279eadf551612f103afda